{"name":"Rainbow’s Outer Rim","hex":"#ff0001","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rainbow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A multicoloured arch in the sky, produced by prismatic refraction of light within droplets of rain in the air.","Any prismatic refraction of light showing a spectrum of colours."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Multicolored, especially if in rainbow order.","Made up of several races or ethnicities, or (more broadly) of several cultural or ideological factions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rainbow"},{"term":"outer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Outside; external.","Farther from the centre of the inside."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outer part.","An uncovered section of the seating at a stadium or sportsground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/outer"},{"term":"rim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nyaturu."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edge around something, especially when circular.","A wheelrim."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rim"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rainbow","blocks":[{"text":"A rainbow is an optical phenomenon caused by refraction, internal reflection and dispersion of light in water droplets resulting in a continuous spectrum of light appearing in the sky. The rainbow takes the form of a multicoloured circular arc. Rainbows caused by sunlight always appear in the section of sky directly opposite the sun. Rainbows can be caused by many forms of airborne water. These include not only rain, but also mist, spray, and airborne dew."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg/330px-Double-alaskan-rainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Double-alaskan-rai